  "notes": [
    "Integration counts are assertions, not independent unit tests or performance measurements. Reruns are not added together.",
    "FCStd/FreeCAD Document is the editable authority. Native geometry uses millimetres; snapshots, quantity rows and exports use SI.",
    "Content revision is a hash; identical authored state restored by Undo has the same revision. New empty category lists are omitted from that hash to retain v0.2.1 compatibility.",
    "The independent command-created GUI fixture uses 200 mm slabs and two front walls; the canonical delivered fixture uses 150 mm slabs and eight walls.",
    "Canonical presentation capture preceded the final proposal-preflight change; fresh GUI reopening and all final building/architecture/exchange GUI suites used the final implementation.",
    "Slab keeps its volume and explicitly cuts Column/Beam; Beam-Column and wall intersections are not deducted. Quantities are per declared element/join rules, not a complete clash-free BOQ.",
    "Normal IFC export explicitly reports full EXPRESS not_requested. Actual canonical full EXPRESS validation passed in Bonsai. Bonsai also uses IfcOpenShell.",
    "Exports are atomic per file with metadata last and caught-failure rollback, not crash-atomic across files. Removed category sidecars can remain on disk; current metadata defines the bundle.",
    "Invalid supported service proposals are checked before opening a mutation transaction to preserve existing Redo. This is not a blanket guarantee for arbitrary raw native Property edits.",
    "Source-only distribution; no FreeCAD, Qt, Blender, Bonsai or IfcOpenShell host/application binaries are redistributed."
  ]
